{
  "base": "2ab355d1",
  "material": "Stationary crystal with \u03bc=K=1, flat H=1 collar about the bore S=R. Both ordered and receiver tag weights assigned from the deep preparation. The material planes remain axially registered for the refit at L=1.",
  "scope": "Normal graph spacing is minimized before releasing one compactly supported axial displacement on the receiving side. Probe has no boundary displacement. Tests either conserve tag weights or keep the full Eulerian exterior order fixed. Kinetic, order-field and carrier/wave energies on the fixed geometry do not change in the Eulerian variation. A full-dimensional free mouth is untested.",
  "registration_gate": "At the ordered cut S=R+H/2 the inherited annular collar has two non-unity hoop stretches r_cut/S; an unstressed continuation using the same crystalline material metric would require unity at that cut. An SO(3)-equivariant diffeomorphism of an initially perforated reference with S>0 cannot cover the fixed-point axis r=0 of the wave pocket. Separate growth or an independently prepared inner core and its static/acoustic junction law can supply missing labels.",
